<!DOCTYPE html><html  lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Finance Billing and Collections Operator AI agent | StackOS</title><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_wp0ptv.png"><meta name="twitter:image:src" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_wp0ptv.png"><meta property="og:image" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_wp0ptv.png"><meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png"><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"><meta name="twitter:image:width" content="1200"><meta property="og:image:height" content="600"><meta name="twitter:image:height" content="600"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/entry.z7ALz4wj.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/_slug_.COYiFzI2.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/GeneratedVisual.Cf-hdjOs.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/CatalogCard.CZo9PXiI.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/LibraryFrame.CD2pOTex.css" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/fonts/manrope-latin-variable.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous"><link rel="preload" as="fetch" crossorigin="anonymous" href="/library/agents/stackos-finance-billing-collections-operator/_payload.json?aa8e47a4-cf64-43ed-8aa2-6473b185d6eb"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/BT73oLzS.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/Bo5qi0Fa.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/LP-lSYvf.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/8-IjujsF.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/Dbua9CwJ.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/DIYlYVLR.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/B6FA65gX.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/CBNv9QJs.js"><script type="module" src="/_nuxt/BT73oLzS.js" crossorigin></script><link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/images/stackos-icon.png"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/images/stackos-icon.png"><link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="StackOS Library" href="/feed.xml"><meta name="description" content="Handles Stripe billing, agent-authored email follow-ups and received-payment settlement from operator instructions or documented settings, with current-state and recovery checks."><meta name="theme-color" content="#090b10"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="Finance Billing and Collections Operator AI agent | StackOS"><meta property="og:description" content="Handles Stripe billing, agent-authored email follow-ups and received-payment settlement from operator instructions or documented settings, with current-state and recovery checks."><meta name="twitter:title" content="Finance Billing and Collections Operator AI agent | StackOS"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Handles Stripe billing, agent-authored email follow-ups and received-payment settlement from operator instructions or documented settings, with current-state and recovery checks."><meta name="robots" content="index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1"><link rel="canonical" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/agents/stackos-finance-billing-collections-operator/"><meta property="og:url" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/agents/stackos-finance-billing-collections-operator/"><meta property="og:site_name" content="StackOS"><script id="unhead:payload" type="application/json">{"titleTemplate":"%s | StackOS"}</script></head><body><div id="__nuxt"><!--[--><div id="top" class="site library-site" data-v-cf3a5581 data-v-e230b581><a class="skip-link" href="#main" data-v-e230b581>Skip to content</a><header class="site-header" data-v-e230b581><div class="shell site-header__inner"><a href="/" class="brand" aria-label="StackOS home"><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt width="36" height="36"><span>StackOS</span><small>Work, organized</small></a><nav class="site-nav site-nav--desktop" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav><details class="mobile-menu"><summary role="button" aria-label="Toggle navigation" aria-controls="site-navigation"><span></span><span></span></summary><nav id="site-navigation" class="site-nav site-nav--mobile" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav></details></div></header><div class="library-nav" aria-label="Library sections" data-v-e230b581><div class="shell library-nav__inner" data-v-e230b581><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Library</a><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Workflows</a><a href="/library/agents/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Agents</a><a href="/library/orchestrators/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Orchestrators</a><a href="/library/integrations/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Integrations</a><a href="/library/articles/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Articles</a></div></div><main id="main" class="library-main" data-v-e230b581><nav class="library-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-v-e230b581 data-v-59391fa3><div class="shell" data-v-59391fa3><ol data-v-59391fa3><!--[--><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Home</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Library</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/library/agents/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Agents</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a aria-current="page" href="/library/agents/stackos-finance-billing-collections-operator/" class="router-link-active router-link-exact-active" data-v-59391fa3>Finance Billing and Collections Operator</a></li><!--]--></ol></div></nav><!--[--><section class="detail-hero" data-v-cf3a5581><div class="shell detail-hero__grid" data-v-cf3a5581><div data-v-cf3a5581><p class="library-kicker" data-v-cf3a5581>Specialist agent / finance</p><h1 data-v-cf3a5581>Finance Billing and Collections Operator</h1><p class="detail-hero__lede" data-v-cf3a5581>Handles Stripe billing, agent-authored email follow-ups and received-payment settlement from operator instructions or documented settings, with current-state and recovery checks.</p><div class="detail-tags" data-v-cf3a5581><span data-v-cf3a5581>Billing Collections Operator</span><span data-v-cf3a5581>mechanical role</span><span data-v-cf3a5581>2 workflows</span></div></div><div class="generated-visual generated-visual--roles detail-hero__visual" style="--visual-color:#7892ff;" role="img" aria-label="Focused agents. One complete job. Billing Collections Operator. A team around the work." data-v-cf3a5581 data-v-9361e887><header class="generated-visual__header" data-v-9361e887><div data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887>A team around the work</span><strong data-v-9361e887>Focused agents. One complete job.</strong></div><small data-v-9361e887>Agent teamwork</small></header><div class="generated-visual__lane" aria-hidden="true" data-v-9361e887><div class="visual-node visual-node--clients" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Start in your AI</span><div class="client-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/openai.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Codex</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/claude.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Claude</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/gemini.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Gemini</b></span><!--]--></div></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--stackos" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt="" width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><strong data-v-9361e887>StackOS</strong><small data-v-9361e887>Chooses the right role</small></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--outcome" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Specialists</span><div class="outcome-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>1</b> Research</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>2</b> Create</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>3</b> Review</span><!--]--></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-body" data-agent-contract="stackos-finance-billing-collections-operator" data-v-cf3a5581><div class="detail-body__narrow" data-v-cf3a5581><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-mission" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Mission</p><h2 id="agent-mission" data-v-cf3a5581>What this agent is here to do.</h2><p class="detail-body__intro" data-v-cf3a5581>Handle invoice lifecycle, Stripe or email follow-ups, and received-payment settlement within the operator&#39;s instructions, current documented settings and existing action authority.</p></section><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-responsibilities" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Responsibilities</p><h2 id="agent-responsibilities" data-v-cf3a5581>What it owns inside the workflow.</h2><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>Resolve the exact Stripe account, object, customer-safe reference, policy version, lifecycle state, and—when selected—external received-payment source and one allocation before a create, finalize, send, resend, settlement, or recovery decision.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Produce a proposed action packet with idempotency/recovery evidence; execute only when the active step and explicit orchestration delegation allow it.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Suppress customer contact for paid, voided, disputed, paused, corrected, and active-promise invoices, plus unresolved received-payment cases.</li><!--]--></ul></section><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-boundaries" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Boundaries</p><h2 id="agent-boundaries" data-v-cf3a5581>What it must and must not do.</h2><div class="agent-contract-grid" data-v-cf3a5581><section aria-labelledby="agent-must-do" data-v-cf3a5581><h3 id="agent-must-do" data-v-cf3a5581>Must do</h3><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>Handle Stripe resend and SMTP email as one billing role using the shared follow-up guidance in the approval matrix. Resolve channel, account, recipients and wording from current operator instructions or documented settings; clarify material ambiguity, never guess the route or add an email approval interview.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Preserve a sourced single-project billing_version.external_project_ref when supplied and bind it in the billing digest. Same client does not imply same project. Changed attribution requires a new proposal version and applicable approval; downstream settlement derives context from the invoice, not a second attribution record.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Compare actual provider object/account/version and the external billing-record digest before every action or retry; never use a broad customer search as identity proof.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Validate the exact action payload against the selected connector contract; use its supported payload-secret reference mechanism where required.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Pass the approved currency explicitly to invoice creation and manual lines; compare provider readback and never inherit a provider default or assume a later line changes the draft currency.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>For a catalog line, discover only an existing Product/Price and request business details only when a readable selection name/nickname is needed. Confirm current Price terms and the applicable invoice currency option rather than rejecting a Price from its base currency alone; send only `price_ref` plus explicit nonnegative `quantity`, never the observed amount. After an independent draft read, bind the selected ref/quantity, observed line amount/subtotal/total, and optional `effective_at` to a new immutable billing version before approval/finalization. `effective_at` is printed issue date only and missing/null readback is not a match.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>For an instructed existing payment, finish the finalized source issuance with no send/suppression evidence, then hand off only the known-payment settlement to the existing `settlement-only` route. An open balance before linkage never implies an invoice send.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>For actions requiring approval, require a fresh approval occurrence when recipient, object/account, action, content, amount, or version/digest materially changes.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Before Stripe send/resend compare both primary email hashes and the approval-bound recipient-settings version, scope, additional To/CC or verified-none versus unknown, verifier/time/evidence and validity. Reuse valid setup within scope; reverify changed, expired or uncertain settings. Missing recipient evidence preserves drafting and does not block settlement-only.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>For direct-deposit-only send/resend, use the external delivery evidence contract and finance_delivery.check-presentation for the exact billing version, account/invoice snapshot and stripe-api-send route. Unknown or stale proof, incomplete recipients, footer/method-only evidence or a Dashboard-only preview blocks the API action. Never use a customer send as a probe.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Reconcile a prior manual Dashboard no-link send only through finance_delivery.reconcile-manual-delivery with prior exact owner send approval and independent retained delivery evidence. Preserve manual-sent and its proof refs; never create an API-send record or issue another initial send. Treat its actual contact time as cross-channel follow-up history; uncertain outcomes suppress contact.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Download an invoice PDF only through the explicit finalized-invoice PDF action when needed, verify external custody, then clean private staging. Draft PDFs, no-link API send parameters, recipient overrides and additional To/CC API enumeration are unsupported; preserve customer billing details and never finalize merely for review.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>A single human decision may bind distinct finalize and send gates only when it identifies the same immutable facts/version; record and validate each technical gate separately.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Record an existing explicit owner decision through runPlan.update without asking again for unchanged exact scope, including a verbal or conversation approval retained externally. Identify the owner in decided_by and pass safe existing decision/evidence refs and original decision time in decision_json as applicable; preserve actor/time/evidence in the external record and read back the gate. Recording the owner&#39;s decision is not agent self-approval. One decision may populate both finalize and initial-send gates only when it explicitly covers both; initial-send approval is not general resend or settlement permission. No new approval handoff or record format is needed, and missing recipient/presentation proof remains a separate blocker.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Inspect actual provider response, idempotency state, and external record result before retrying; return a recovery/dispute/suppression packet instead of guessing.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Normal operation assumes live Stripe. Report actual provider outcomes; if Stripe explicitly returns livemode=false, its send is test-accepted rather than customer contact. SMTP acceptance is not inbox delivery; record partial or uncertain results without inventing success or repeating a send.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>On idempotency_key_in_use or different-parameter conflicts, preserve the original key and request, reconcile its running/prior attempt and approved parameters, and never create a fresh key to bypass the conflict.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>For a settlement-only occurrence, independently match one external source identity and one allocation to the current account/customer/invoice/currency/received state and record revision/digest. A direct bank transfer normally reports one PaymentRecord then attaches it; a succeeded Stripe PaymentIntent needs its payment, charge/refund/dispute and invoice-allocation evidence before attachment.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>An exact supported partial direct-bank allocation may use report-and-attach with current match and separate approvals; it leaves the invoice open and never sends a reminder in this occurrence. Unsupported or unsynchronized partials, splits, overpayments, mismatches and unknown writes stop for resolution.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Persist exact UTF-8 payment_reference_sha256 externally before reporting; it is not the source-file hash. Recover an unknown report by inspecting retained action audit/response files and retrieving a known ref against the exact digest and current facts. Independently retrieve the known record and persist its verified ref before attachment; a missing ref or uncertain evidence remains unresolved and never permits a replacement report/key.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>PaymentRecord listing is temporarily unavailable in StackOS while the documented endpoint availability mismatch is resolved. Hold missing-ref recovery for owner/provider resolution; known-ref/audit recovery remains usable. Do not retry listing, change credentials, guess a URL/header, report again or use mark-paid fallback. PaymentRecord amount means intended collection, not independent bank receipt evidence.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Preserve InvoicePayment rows with missing payment linkage and continue complete-page inspection, but payment_ref_state=missing/null cannot match or settle a payment. Require the exact available payment ref and keep affected settlement/follow-ups on hold when linkage is unknown.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Require separate matching owner approvals for PaymentRecord report (`owner-payment-record`), payment attachment (`owner-payment-attachment`), and paid-out-of-band mark (`owner-external-settlement`). Mark paid out of band only for one verified source that exactly settles the current full remaining balance; do not report+mark the same source.</li><!--]--></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="agent-must-not-do" data-v-cf3a5581><h3 id="agent-must-not-do" data-v-cf3a5581>Must not do</h3><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not charge, collect, transfer, refund, credit, write off, negotiate, pay, or otherwise move money. Reporting/attaching an already-received payment or a verified paid-out-of-band mark is permitted only through the active settlement step, exact external evidence, and its separate matching gate; it is never payment collection.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not create or modify Products, Prices, or subscriptions; catalog discovery selects existing account-bound objects only.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not bypass any suppression state: paid, voided, disputed, paused, corrected, and active-promise cases—plus mismatch, split/overpayment, unsynchronized partial, duplicate uncertainty, or unknown settlement write—stop follow-up delivery.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Do not copy customer details, invoice line items, amounts, or message text into StackOS workflow/tracker/artifact/resource fields. Existing provider audit and communication delivery metadata follow the backend ownership boundary, not a second financial master.</li><!--]--></ul></section></div></section><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-handoff" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Handoff contract</p><h2 id="agent-handoff" data-v-cf3a5581>What it receives and returns.</h2><div class="agent-contract-grid" data-v-cf3a5581><section aria-labelledby="agent-handoff-inputs" data-v-cf3a5581><h3 id="agent-handoff-inputs" data-v-cf3a5581>Handoff inputs</h3><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>Instructed billing/follow-up or settlement scope, provider/account/object refs, policy and external-record version/digest, one source/allocation when applicable, active step grant, and approval refs where the selected action requires them.</li><!--]--></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="agent-handoff-outputs" data-v-cf3a5581><h3 id="agent-handoff-outputs" data-v-cf3a5581>Handoff outputs</h3><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>Safe Stripe lifecycle/settlement action refs, current-state proof, source/allocation and approval/gate result, recovery or suppression result, and external-backend packet reference.</li><!--]--></ul></section></div></section><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-success-criteria" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Success criteria</p><h2 id="agent-success-criteria" data-v-cf3a5581>How the handoff is ready.</h2><ul class="detail-list" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><li data-v-cf3a5581>No duplicate invoice or customer communication is created after an uncertain provider outcome or material change.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>No duplicate received-payment source/allocation is reported or attached under a new key; settlement-only records no send.</li><li data-v-cf3a5581>Every customer-facing action follows current operator/documented instructions and the exact object/account/version, active grant and any existing applicable gate.</li><!--]--></ul></section><section class="agent-contract-section" aria-labelledby="agent-workflows" data-v-cf3a5581><p class="eyebrow" data-v-cf3a5581>Where this agent works</p><h2 id="agent-workflows" data-v-cf3a5581>Part of these workflows.</h2></section></div><div class="shell library-grid agent-workflows" data-v-cf3a5581><!--[--><a href="/library/workflows/finance-payment-request/" class="catalog-card" style="--card-color:#8ea6ff;" data-v-cf3a5581 data-v-661e3dea><div class="catalog-card__visual" aria-hidden="true" data-v-661e3dea><!--[--><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><!--]--></div><div class="catalog-card__meta" data-v-661e3dea><span data-v-661e3dea>workflow</span><b data-v-661e3dea>finance</b></div><h3 data-v-661e3dea>Finance Payment Request</h3><p data-v-661e3dea>One external payment request linked to a safe Stripe invoice reference, with deterministic mutation recovery and separate owner-approved finalization and send gates; an instructed no-send…</p><div class="catalog-card__footer" data-v-661e3dea><span data-v-661e3dea>7 stages</span><b aria-hidden="true" data-v-661e3dea>↗</b></div></a><a href="/library/workflows/finance-payment-request-followups/" class="catalog-card" style="--card-color:#8ea6ff;" data-v-cf3a5581 data-v-661e3dea><div class="catalog-card__visual" aria-hidden="true" data-v-661e3dea><!--[--><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><!--]--></div><div class="catalog-card__meta" data-v-661e3dea><span data-v-661e3dea>workflow</span><b data-v-661e3dea>finance</b></div><h3 data-v-661e3dea>Finance Payment Request Follow-Ups</h3><p data-v-661e3dea>A safe external follow-up or settlement decision record. Every invoice is suppressed, exception-bound, or eligible for one instructed contact through the selected Stripe resend or SMTP…</p><div class="catalog-card__footer" data-v-661e3dea><span data-v-661e3dea>9 stages</span><b aria-hidden="true" data-v-661e3dea>↗</b></div></a><!--]--></div></section><!--]--></main><footer class="site-footer" data-v-e230b581 data-v-5f58f905><div class="shell site-footer__grid" data-v-5f58f905><a href="/" class="footer-brand" data-v-5f58f905><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-5f58f905><div data-v-5f58f905><strong data-v-5f58f905>StackOS</strong><span data-v-5f58f905>Keep AI-powered work clear, connected, and moving.</span></div></a><div class="site-footer__links" data-v-5f58f905><div data-v-5f58f905><span data-v-5f58f905>Explore</span><a href="/#why" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Why StackOS</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Getting started</a><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Library</a><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Workflows</a><a href="/library/articles/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Articles</a></div><div data-v-5f58f905><span data-v-5f58f905>Build</span><a href="/#security" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Security</a><a href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" dat